Installed `MessageActions` (`@/components/ui/message-actions`) with its styles, upstream's own icon glyphs and emoji data. The "icons" style (`message-actions-icons-*`) draws the same icons from Lucide or Phosphor instead.

```tsx
import { MessageActions } from "@/components/ui/message-actions";

<MessageActions
  text={message.text}
  sentAt={message.createdAt}
  onVote={(vote) => saveVote(message.id, vote)}
  onReact={(emoji) => saveReaction(message.id, emoji)}
/>
```

Pass `density="comfortable"` for 24px touch and pointer targets (WCAG 2.2 target size); the default keeps upstream's tighter 20px buttons.

The row renders its own stylesheet (hoisted into `<head>` once by React 19); its colors are `--message-actions-*` variables on `.message-actions-root` and on the popups (`.message-actions-surface`), with a dark set under `.dark`, `[data-theme="dark"]` or the system dark scheme.

Ported from Message Actions in AICSS by Kevin (kvnkld) (MIT); the license notice is at the end of every file.
